### =====================================================================
### Detection rule triggers — dev testing
###
### Thresholds below match your rules as built:
###   BruteForceRule      threshold 10, window 10 min  (>=10 AUTH_FAILURE from one IP)
###   PasswordSprayingRule threshold 10, window 10 min (>=10 DISTINCT principals from one IP)
###   KeyIdorRule          threshold 10, window 10 min (>=10 AUTHZ_IDOR from one IP)
###
### If you change a rule's threshold(), change the repeat count here to match.
### All requests come from 127.0.0.1, so every rule groups them under one entity.
### =====================================================================

@host = http://localhost:8080
@goodPassword = SuperSecret123
@wrongPassword = definitely-wrong-password


### =====================================================================
### SETUP — run once. Creates the victim + the attacker.
### =====================================================================

### victim: owns the API key that gets probed in the KEY_IDOR section
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "victim@test.local",
  "username": "victim_user",
  "displayName": "Victim User",
  "password": "{{goodPassword}}"
}

### attacker: does the probing
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "attacker@test.local",
  "username": "attacker_user",
  "displayName": "Attacker User",
  "password": "{{goodPassword}}"
}


### =====================================================================
### BRUTE_FORCE — 11 failed logins, SAME email, one IP.
### Rule counts COUNT(*) of AUTH_FAILURE per IP. 11 > threshold 10.
### Run all 11 in under 10 minutes or they fall out of the window.
