### =====================================================================
### KEY_IDOR — 11 attempts to revoke a key you don't own.
### Each rejected attempt publishes AUTHZ_IDOR from AuthzService.
###
### /api/keys is cookie-authenticated and NOT CSRF-exempt, so the DELETEs
### must echo the XSRF-TOKEN cookie back as a header. The login handlers
### below capture it automatically.
### =====================================================================

### 1. login as VICTIM and capture their CSRF token
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "victim@test.local", "password": "{{goodPassword}}"}

> {%
    const c = response.headers.valuesOf("Set-Cookie").find(h => h.startsWith("XSRF-TOKEN="));
    if (c) client.global.set("xsrf", c.split(";")[0].split("=")[1]);
%}

### 2. victim creates a key — capture its id as the IDOR target
POST {{host}}/api/keys
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}

{"label": "victim-key", "scopes": "ALERTS_READ"}

> {%
    client.global.set("victimKeyId", response.body.data.apiKeyDTO.id);
    client.log("victim key id = " + client.global.get("victimKeyId"));
%}

### 3. login as ATTACKER (replaces the session cookie + captures their CSRF token)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "attacker@test.local", "password": "{{goodPassword}}"}

> {%
    const c = response.headers.valuesOf("Set-Cookie").find(h => h.startsWith("XSRF-TOKEN="));
    if (c) client.global.set("xsrf", c.split(";")[0].split("=")[1]);
%}

### 4-14. attacker probes the victim's key 11 times — each should be 403 + AUTHZ_IDOR
DELETE {{host}}/api/keys/{{victimKeyId}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/keys/{{victimKeyId}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}

###
